    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p3_b11",
      "text": "Visual Instruction Tuning (VIT). Modern LVLMs undergo\na two-stage training process: an initial Pre-Training (PT)\nfor coarse alignment on large-scale image-text pairs, fol-\nlowed by Visual Instruction Tuning (VIT) for fine-grained\nalignment on high-quality instruction data. Our analysis fo-\ncuses on the VIT stage, as pre-trained models are typically\nlimited to generating a series of short, descriptive phrases\nand exhibit minimal language bias (Figure 10).\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        309.06,
        543.1,
        402.72
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        1236,
        2172,
        1610
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.86,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 458,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p3_b12",
