    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p3_b18",
      "text": "Direct Preference Optimization (DPO). DPO (Rafailov\net al., 2024) aligns models with human preferences directly\nfrom preference data, offering a more streamlined alter-\nnative to Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback\n(RLHF) (Stiennon et al., 2020; Ouyang et al., 2022), which\noften requires a separate and complex reward model. In the\nmultimodal setting, DPO utilizes a preference dataset D of\ntuples (x, v, yw, yl), containing a prompt x, an image v, a\npreferred response (yw), and a less preferred one (yl). The\noptimization objective is:\n",
